ProsperoSunshine: sunshine.conf sets how the video is paced for clients over the internet

Patch 0026 paces large frames for a client over the internet (video/frame_pacing.hpp). Two of its numbers depend on the path
and can now be set: internet_pace_percent, how fast the part of a large frame beyond the burst leaves, in percent of the
stream's rate (200 by default, 125 to 800), and internet_burst_kb, the most of a frame that leaves at once (16 by default,
2 to 64). A value out of range keeps the default. Issue 37's reporter streams over ps5-tailscale, which relays from the
console itself; at 1080p and 15 Mbit/s the pace of 0.6.5 (four times the rate, 32 kB at once) was more than that path
took.

--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -421,6 +421,8 @@
   struct ps5_t {
     bool close_game_on_quit;  ///< Moonlight's Terminate App closes the session's game too (off by default).
     bool pair_over_internet;  ///< Pairing requests from outside the LAN and Tailscale are answered (off by default).
+    int internet_pace_percent;  ///< Clients over the internet: the rest of a large frame leaves at this percent of the stream's rate.
+    int internet_burst_kb;  ///< Clients over the internet: the most of a frame that leaves at once, in kB.
   };
 
   extern ps5_t ps5;
